[{"text":"It is not hard to guess that the scalar product is SP","anchor":"cb10-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"SP[p, q]","anchor":"cb11","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"while for the metric tensor we write MT","anchor":"cb11-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"MT[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]]","anchor":"cb12","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{g}^{\\mu \\nu }\\]","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"To input a Dirac matrix or a Feynman slash, use GA or GS respectively","anchor":"cb12-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"GA[\\[Mu]]","anchor":"cb13","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"GS[p]","anchor":"cb14","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{p}\\]","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"The Levi-Civita tensor is LC","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Sigma]]","anchor":"cb15","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"The fully contracted form is entered via","anchor":"cb15-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"LC[][p1, p2, q1, q2]","anchor":"cb16","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{q1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{q2}}}\\]","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"It is also possible to enter a mixed form","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu]][p1, p2, q]","anchor":"cb17","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\overline{q}}\\]","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu], \\[Nu]][p1, p2]","anchor":"cb18","section":"External representation"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p2}}}\\]","anchor":"cb18-1","section":"External representation"},{"text":"To convert between the two representations we use the functions FCI and FCE, which are shortcuts for FeynCalcInternal and FeynCalcExternal. One cannot distinguish between the notations using the typesetting, i.e. when we see a typeset object in the TraditionalForm, we cannot really tell if it is in the FCI or FCE notation.","anchor":"switching-between-the-representations","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"ex1 = FV[p, \\[Mu]] ex2 = Pair[Momentum[p], LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]]]","anchor":"cb19","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"However, we can always use StandardForm to see the difference","anchor":"cb19-2","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"ex1 // StandardForm ex2 // StandardForm (*FV[p, \\[Mu]]*) (*Pair[LorentzIndex[\\[Mu]], Momentum[p]]*)","anchor":"cb20","section":"Switching between the representations"},{"text":"All FeynCalc functions that are meant for users will automatically convert the user input in the FCE notation into the FCI notation. You do not have to do it by yourself.","anchor":"why-it-matters","section":"Why it matters"},{"text":"On the other hand, virtually all FeynCalc functions produce their output in the FCI form. So when you have an expression that was obtained from FeynCalc and want to apply some replacement rules to it, we have to use the FCI form in the rule","anchor":"why-it-matters","section":"Why it matters"},{"text":"ex = Pair[Momentum[p], Momentum[q]]","anchor":"cb21","section":"Why it matters"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb21-1","section":"Why it matters"}]